/-!
# Controlled copy evolution

This module constructs `controlledCopyChannel` by adjoining a density copy, applying a
controlled partial swap, and tracing out the copy. Boolean control coordinates are related to
the encoded register `Fin (2 * D)`, and `copyControlledEvolution` is identified with evolution
generated by `controlledCopyHamiltonian`.

The estimates quantify the controlled density-matrix exponentiation construction of
[LloydMohseniRebentrost2014]. With an arbitrary reference register, one step has trace-norm
error at most eight times the squared angle times the input trace; `controlledCopyRun`
accumulates an error bounded by `8 * t ^ 2 / n` times the input trace for positive `n`.

## Main statements

* `controlledCopyChannelMap_relabel`: compatibility of raw and encoded control coordinates.
* `copyControlledEvolution_hamiltonian`: the controlled Hamiltonian representation.
* `controlled_copy_fresh_global_error`: the reference-register error bound for repeated steps.
* `controlled_copy_actual_cptp_and_false_block`: the channel fixes the false control sector.

## References

* [Lloyd, Mohseni, and Rebentrost, 2014][LloydMohseniRebentrost2014]
-/

